From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shaders/colorspace: read the Dolby Vision MMR order as an int

reshape_mmr() declares the order of an MMR piece as a uint and then
compares it with the literals 2 and 3. GLSL ES has no implicit conversion
from int to uint, so those comparisons are not valid there, and the shader
of such a picture would not compile on an OpenGL ES context, which is what
Kodi has on GBM. The order is 1, 2 or 3 either way.

The line is only written for a component that has MMR pieces of different
orders. No stream seen so far has one, which is why this never failed: for
every other picture the text of the shader does not change.

Origin: the Intel Dolby Vision LibreELEC fork, CroqueMr/libreelec-x86-DV,
R1.0.0 Beta2 (commit 2e2fc3e954bb808daf3472250c0f7dc3f301fe5f), file
CB1/patches/libplacebo/libplacebo-9912-native-transport.patch, which has
this change among others. The others are left out: they make the text of
the shader depend on the values of the coefficients (more programs for one
stream, compiled while it plays), change what the scaler computes, or have
to be asked for by a caller.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, that of libplacebo and of the file changed,
whose notice stays as it is.
---
 src/shaders/colorspace.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/shaders/colorspace.c b/src/shaders/colorspace.c
--- a/src/shaders/colorspace.c
+++ b/src/shaders/colorspace.c
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@

     assert(min_order <= max_order);
     if (min_order < max_order)
-        GLSL("uint order = uint(coeffs.w); \n");
+        GLSL("int order = int(coeffs.w); \n");

     GLSL("vec4 sigX;                            \n"
          "s = coeffs.x;                         \n"
